## Image Tags — Pinning Specific Versions

On Docker Hub, every image can have multiple **tags** — think of tags as version labels.

```bash
docker pull redis          # pulls "latest" tag by default
docker pull redis:7.2      # pulls specifically version 7.2
docker pull redis:bullseye # pulls a Debian Bullseye-based variant
```

This maps directly to what you did in your Lambda project:
```dockerfile
FROM public.ecr.aws/lambda/python:3.12
#                                 ^^^^
#                              This is the tag — Python 3.12 specifically
```

If you had written `FROM public.ecr.aws/lambda/python` with no tag, Docker would have pulled `latest` — which could change unexpectedly. **Always pin tags in production.**

