## Connecting This to Your Lambda Work

Your ECR + Lambda workflow was exactly this pattern, just on AWS infrastructure:

| Local Docker | Your Lambda Setup |
|---|---|
| `docker pull` from Docker Hub | Lambda pulls your image from **ECR** |
| `docker run -d` | Lambda **runs your container** on invocation |
| `-p 80:80` port mapping | Lambda handles networking — exposes your function via its own endpoint |
| `docker stop` | Lambda tears down the container after execution |
| `docker images` | ECR stores and versions your images |

The only difference: on your laptop you manage containers manually. On AWS Lambda, the entire lifecycle — pull, run, stop, scale — is managed automatically by AWS.

