## Quick Reference Cheat Sheet

```bash
docker -v                          # check Docker version
docker images                      # list all local images
docker ps                          # list running containers
docker ps -a                       # list all containers (inc. stopped)

docker pull <image>                # download image from Docker Hub
docker run <image>                 # run image as container (foreground)
docker run -d <image>              # run in detached (background) mode
docker run -d -p HOST:CONTAINER <image>  # run with port mapping

docker stop <container_id>         # gracefully stop a container
docker rm <container_id>           # remove a stopped container
docker image remove <image_id>     # delete an image
docker image remove -f <image_id>  # force delete (bypasses link errors)
```